    [BugFix][MRV2] Use compiler config for static kernel initialization (#19245)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    MRV2 profiling can reach static kernel initialization without an active
    current-vLLM-config context, causing:
    `AssertionError: Current vLLM config is not set.`
    
    Use `self.vllm_config`, already supplied by `compute_hash()`, instead of
    `get_current_vllm_config()`. This matches the existing `compile()` and
    cache-miss `load()` paths. Remove the unused import; no fallback or
    worker changes.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Fixes the missing-current-config startup failure when MRV2 and static
    kernels are enabled. No new configuration options.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    Tested on MRV2 offline inference example.
    
    Follow-up to #19177; related to #19176.
    
    ### Checklist
    - [ ] Automated regression test added
    - [ ] Full MRV2 hardware startup validation completed
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/a98247ab4db686ee03c66d5feb3c761e52a2f8ab
    
